		(uuid "acec0423-40f4-4ece-ac52-7efba0d3085f")
	)
	(text "Motor Specs (From polulu's website)\nvoltage: 6V\nno-load performance: 1100RPM, 150mA\nstall extrapolation: 0.45 kg⋅cm (6.2 oz⋅in), 1.5 A"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 30.988 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "bfbd6434-b2a9-451d-9d62-bcc9fc63095b")
	)
	(text "3. Add Mounting holes as needed for the motors!\nFor mounting holes, use M2! \n(Standard size, stands for 2mm diameter screw holes)\nThere are KiCAD footprints for M2, you can \"place component\" in the schematic."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 125.73 228.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d5878c54-d406-4344-9010-a4c4fbbf52be")
	)
	(text "Recall how we breadboarded circuits for the emitter and the receiver!\nFor the emitter, you can choose to use either the SFH4545 or the TSAL6100.\nFootprints for both emitters should be in our custom KiCAD library.\n(If not, you can find footprints and import them from SnapEDA!)\n\nFor more on the IR sensor geometry layout side, \nwe will be making a separate google doc guide!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.718 169.164 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d852bc75-f2a4-446f-a5e1-89b4532db1d3")
	)
	(text "1. You should add indicator LEDs! Think about how to design the circuit...\nAlso, debugging LEDs if you have extra pins would be helpful."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 125.984 195.326 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "de743563-91c8-455c-9469-c892296bfc96")
	)
	(text "Use two 1*6 pinConnector components (one for each motor)\nand assign the pin order based on what the polulu website shows!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 38.608 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "df701be8-d9d6-4dae-a04b-054bc34f1c2c")
	)
	(text "Motors with Encoders - Connectors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.954 20.828 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e91b821e-72a7-485f-9e36-e56251d02747")
	)
	(text "Notes on L7805\nOutput current up to 1.5 A\n• Thermal overload protection\n• Short circuit protection\n• Output transition SOA protection\n• 2 % output voltage tolerance (A version)\n• Guaranteed in extended temperature range (A version)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 29.972 114.808 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f4bc7959-10bb-40e9-8ef5-10516a087293")
	)
	(text "Go to File->Page Settings to change the sheet name to your bot's name!"
